  "scope": "Ignore first/last histogram bins in all eighteen image threshold methods, six ImageJ histogram methods, C++ overloads/Python API and the shared native Auto Threshold form. Defaults remain off; existing C++ overloads remain available.",
  "behavior": "Exclusions affect threshold estimation only; the complete source image participates in the output mask. The histogram input and source samples are preserved. Empty eligible histograms refuse and failed jobs never publish. Options are recorded and survive workflow serialization/replay, preview/cancel, Apply and undo/redo. Invalid nonboolean flags refuse. Endpoint exclusion requires finite samples and 2..65536 bins; the six histogram methods enforce the effective eligible count limit INT32_MAX.",
  "compatibility": "The two existing C++ histogram/image overload families remain source-callable. With both flags off, old method conventions are retained; mean continues to use the raw sample mean. When exclusion is requested, mean uses the eligible histogram weighted bin-center mean. Full reference parity of the twelve older methods is still open. Min-error/moments fallback to Otsu retains the requested flags.",
